#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Listen for the wake word and carry out spoken commands.

Everything runs on the Pi. openWakeWord listens for the wake word, Moonshine
(through sherpa-onnx) turns the command into text, everyday commands are
matched straight away and anything else goes to a small language model in
llama-server (cannvas-llm.service), and Piper speaks the reply through the TV.
Audio only lives in memory, from the wake word until the command has been
transcribed, and nothing is sent off the Pi except the Home Assistant calls the
command asks for.

It runs as a user service beside the kiosk because it needs the desktop's
PipeWire session for the USB microphone and the TV's speakers. The kiosk page
follows along through /events (server-sent events) on a loopback port, which
cannvas-server proxies as /api/voice/events.
"""

